# The database must never enter the build context as a raw file: it is ~1 GB and
# lives on the Railway volume.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*
*.csv
.git/
*.bak
__pycache__/
README.md

# seed/ is deliberately NOT excluded. It is how the volume gets seeded: a
# COMPRESSED database is shipped in the image once, entrypoint.sh decompresses it
# onto the volume on first boot, and then seed/ is deleted and the service is
# redeployed so later code deploys stay small. See seed-image.sh.

# tools/ is the verification harness (column census, output-equality diff, route
# capture). Useful in the repo, pointless in the runtime image.
tools/
